<div class="columnArticleClass two-layout-bg-white" id="oneColumnArticleTheme"><div class="text-start container multitextblock "><div class="row justify-content-left"><div class="col col-md-8"><h2>Why Distributed Controller?</h2><p>Distributed Controllers are used for machines with a distributed architecture and for series machines with limited space available. By relocating intelligence to individual stations, you can fix faults without the plant grinding to a standstill, increasing availability. They combine the advantages of a SIMATIC S7-1500 with the design of a SIMATIC ET 200 IO system. </p><p>Distributed Controllers can be mounted directly on the machine in small control boxes or, in the case of the ET 200pro, without them. In networked plants, connection to a production line&#x27;s central control cabinet is realized via PROFINET. Moving data from the central control cabinet to Distributed Controllers on the individual stations improves overall availability.</p><p>Our Distributed Controllers include:</p><ul><li>SIMATIC ET 200SP Open Controller</li><li>SIMATIC ET 200SP CPUs</li><li>SIMATIC ET 200pro CPUs</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><div id='2VqmQoaXFfYAWxzO9soSF3' class='sitesThreeColTiles themed-component-wrapper' data-ste-section='three-col-tiles_3' data-ste-section-id='2VqmQoaXFfYAWxzO9soSF3'>
